Discovered and source-validated recurrence for `factorial`.

```python
def factorial(n):
    return 1 if (n == 0) else (n * factorial(n - 1))

print(factorial(10))
```

Result for factorial(10): 3628800

How it works: the cached abstract definition was formalized into a boundary condition and a transition whose n measure strictly decreases on every recursive call.
